    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0790" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg696"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 107.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    just received a telegram of which the following is a copy: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>American schooner <hi rendition="#italic">William Todd</hi>, en route
                            Mobile here, fired on [by] Spanish gunboats off Isle Pines before flag
                            hoisted. Afterwards searched; futile. Report mailed.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eckford</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Kingston.</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <pb facs="0791" n="697" xml:id="pg697"/>
                <p>I shall communicate with you further upon the receipt of the report referred
                    to.</p>
                <p>I give you this notice of telegram received, that you may cause such
                    investigation to be set on foot as you may think proper.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
